2RuKUW8BY1h8AxmLZgfnMQ52m41YaLEFjM/mpRXZ2Feagq+J67S6J9WNHNLyAqFHyW+5Y6ZWMUnh/x+KXFS6RWwqubGAQ=","title":"WildFeedback: Aligning LLMs With In-situ User Interactions And Feedback","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2408.15549"}]},{"type":"text","text":", so long task-shaped sessions are rare.\n  - LMSYS-Chat-1M — ","nativeMessageIdx":3},{"type":"text","text":"1M real-user conversations from the Vicuna demo and Chatbot Arena across 25 models","nativeMessageIdx":3,"citations":[{"type":"web_search_citation","cited_text":"[107] introduced LMSYS-Chat-1M, a million-scale dataset of realuser conversations collected in the wild via the Vicuna demo and the well-known Chatbot...","encrypted_index":"EpABCioIExgCIiRkNTg3NDcwNC1iMWQxLTQ3YmYtYTFhMC1jNWI5MDRkZjA0ZjgSDEAqI5607JwZ83HkmRoMY0EtdHVy+z1Axh3qIjBCRQXya5s3oYvvljf/zVuIHzNpL38JvA1eJse4K+T+ZZsuR0gDzvBCG6PTPSV+WdwqFKciXpGFZkqHgVQisnhpuhHHQWlfGAQ=","title":"Priming, Path-dependence, and Plasticity: Understanding the molding of user-LLM interaction and its implications from (many) chat logs in the wild","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2605.05767"}]},{"type":"text","text":", but ","nativeMessageIdx":3},{"type":"text","text":"users there are evaluating models rather than pursuing real needs","nativeMessageIdx":3,"citations":[{"type":"web_search_citation","cited_text":"LMSYS-chat-1M (Zheng et al., 2023a) is collected from Chatbot Arena,<sup>4</sup> where users interact with LLMs to *evaluate* them. ","encrypted_index":"EpABCioIExgCIiRkNTg3NDcwNC1iMWQxLTQ3YmYtYTFhMC1jNWI5MDRkZjA0ZjgSDFpp1SeDfBdD9P80QBoMisNhRhdUJdcR8FUcIjBT1HpLMKOc6N4DFhCzQMzlCx6q6/9p6KxUK7PFexFkOL6VlYaJZ6KkoRY6lTEEYMIqFF9JZxaaT+I3JKIQrts5U1dKGc3JGAQ=","title":"User Feedback in Human-LLM Dialogues: A Lens to Understand Users But Noisy as a Learning Signal","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2507.23158"},{"type":"web_search_citation","cited_text":"LMSYS is used mainly for model evaluation, while WildChat more closely reflects real user needs.","encrypted_index":"EpABCioIExgCIiRkNTg3NDcwNC1iMWQxLTQ3YmYtYTFhMC1jNWI5MDRkZjA0ZjgSDCMAXsNCg80LbYB4+RoMVrmLEg3ZDhkRDn+QIjBUbIDV6z/h0XHlsGd+mQjRpFw1UJgVLiguT798+6DlriLqp4Us9I94Bojmmes+yAIqFNUeNBpjG0O+HO0LsgvubFz+lQMNGAQ=","title":"User Feedback in Human-LLM Dialogues: A Lens to Understand Users But Noisy as a Learning Signal","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2507.23158"}]},{"type":"text","text":", so ecological validity is worse than WildChat for your purposes.\n  - Useful for finding candidates: WildVis, ","nativeMessageIdx":3},{"type":"text","text":"an interactive tool for exploring million-scale chat logs, MIT-licensed with a live demo at wildvisualizer.com","nativeMessageIdx":3,"citations":[{"type":"web_search_citation","cited_text":"WILDVIS, an interactive tool for exploring millionscale chat logs. \n\n","encrypted_index":"EpABCioIExgCIiRkNTg3NDcwNC1iMWQxLTQ3YmYtYTFhMC1jNWI5MDRkZjA0ZjgSDHewOlesuNNQapJTKRoMVRDM6HF8p/Z7fEavIjB779gNr9oVMLgGeoWymujzZueo3r6ytQQH6Tm6pP/ay87v0Z/2BTfCRQkMD1aimrsqFBuJMRdB/K0k98qOI04NyDVekI4fGAQ=","title":"WildVis: Open Source Visualizer for Million-Scale Chat Logs in the Wild","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2409.03753"},{"type":"web_search_citation","cited_text":"As an open-source project, WILDVIS is available at github.com/da03/WildVisualizer under an MIT license, and a working demo can be accessed at wildvisu...","encrypted_index":"EpEBCioIExgCIiRkNTg3NDcwNC1iMWQxLTQ3YmYtYTFhMC1jNWI5MDRkZjA0ZjgSDAtfoZOg0idntQTuFBoMohDniROgg9sKjv1NIjAD9eL+lM5s+lGjjvYtTCa//a8lvXouhYnbRLS5wtR2Hmakkw3DU1m3cAWePv8P2p8qFXAadplsWh3+vfO3MKytPqzrE8KNMRgE","title":"WildVis: Open Source Visualizer for Million-Scale Chat Logs in the Wild","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2409.03753"}]},{"type":"text","text":". ","nativeMessageIdx":3},{"type":"text","text":"It supports compositional filters like keyword plus minimum turn count","nativeMessageIdx":3,"citations":[{"type":"web_search_citation","cited_text":"This example demonstrates the application of multiple criteria, including the keyword \"Election,\" conversations with more than two turns, and chats fr...","encrypted_index":"EpABCioIExgCIiRkNTg3NDcwNC1iMWQxLTQ3YmYtYTFhMC1jNWI5MDRkZjA0ZjgSDI44XraOrkDSXa9FhhoMkXIFTlkpzNyB+hqcIjDa8kC8dKJ/lX5Re2eUqpGpnPwwkc1Z6qjZv/4+grvUaZzUagg5VLYfZSnNOwq0oJUqFMtG/8dM2EWJzxRERLHAMhsAzTiBGAQ=","title":"WildVis: Open Source Visualizer for Million-Scale Chat Logs in the Wild","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2409.03753"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — exactly what you'd use to pull long multi-turn sessions in a domain where the user is clearly out of their depth.\n  - There's also prior work mining this data for your exact phenomenon: ","nativeMessageIdx":3},{"type":"text","text":"a study of \"interaction smells\" in multi-turn human-LLM collaborative code generation built on WildChat and LMSYS-Chat-1M","nativeMessageIdx":3,"citations":[{"type":"web_search_citation","cited_text":"## 3 Study Design\n\n#### 3.1 Datasets\n\n**Wildchat** [46] is a comprehensive multi-turn, multilingual dataset comprising a corpus of 1 million user-Chat...","encrypted_index":"EpABCioIExgCIiRkNTg3NDcwNC1iMWQxLTQ3YmYtYTFhMC1jNWI5MDRkZjA0ZjgSDAkyjDd4CWxJUIDrgxoMhOWjHjqL4Uv3zfkUIjBcsbEjTjlljud6tvTekGpr3hVrk46Mkz+SBwM+6kXaFw9kkynOVndeTyW8C2dPSbMqFMqfnN+Z0oq/OVVPd48geeBodr9NGAQ=","title":"An Empirical Study of Interaction Smells in Multi-Turn Human-LLM Collaborative Code Generation","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2603.09701"},{"type":"web_search_citation","cited_text":"**LMSYS-CHAT-1M** [47] is a large-scale, real-world LLM conversation dataset containing 1 million dialogues with 25 SOTA LLMs, covering over 150 langu...","encrypted_index":"EpABCioIExgCIiRkNTg3NDcwNC1iMWQxLTQ3YmYtYTFhMC1jNWI5MDRkZjA0ZjgSDHqJCGEquiyAsRf//hoMIawqti5hE+hEBB81IjBbTnT37LMP4FHF07vQhjLyJk3ATAtp3d2iZ/G0LEjcFlvJHqo8NGJ85wCgMVChd4sqFCm/6aVFKqMyl6qmlLf+1i+5xVDYGAQ=","title":"An Empirical Study of Interaction Smells in Multi-Turn Human-LLM Collaborative Code Generation","url":"https://arxiv.org/pd
f/2603.09701"}]},{"type":"text","text":". Their smell taxonomy is probably a decent shortlist of the moments prototype 2 should surface.\n\n- Tool use, no real human:\n  - ","nativeMessageIdx":3},{"type":"text","text":"Nebius SWE-rebench OpenHands trajectories","nativeMessageIdx":3,"citations":[{"type":"web_search_citation","cited_text":"To our knowledge, no other publicly available agent trajectory dataset includes evaluation of agent-generated tests. ","encrypted_index":"Eo8BCioIExgCIiRkNTg3NDcwNC1iMWQxLTQ3YmYtYTFhMC1jNWI5MDRkZjA0ZjgSDHtf1LkBdmVpz0SPHBoMhXw9VWOir4f+mPanIjCoQxrgePep4ODLb9MtSbO0OgGN6He7jmTJUxfURug4yy0KmGd1qTwD9r+YIuWyv00qE+GE8wkiuoK23/0tXB/C10r9dA0YBA==","title":"nebius/SWE-rebench-openhands-trajectories · Datasets at Hugging Face","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/nebius/SWE-rebench-openhands-trajectories"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — real agent runs on real repos, but agent-solo.\n  - ","nativeMessageIdx":3},{"type":"text","text":"AgentTrove, 1.7M rows in terminus-2 ShareGPT-style layout where each row is a complete trajectory including tool calls, environment responses, and final reasoning","nativeMessageIdx":3,"citations":[{"type":"web_search_citation","cited_text":"At 1.7 million rows, AgentTrove is 4× the size of the Nemotron Terminal Corpus (430 K rows), the previous largest open-source agentic trace dataset. C...","encrypted_index":"EpEBCioIExgCIiRkNTg3NDcwNC1iMWQxLTQ3YmYtYTFhMC1jNWI5MDRkZjA0ZjgSDAmzvLxOCABXODIaXhoMpM3SdN/oC4gT/yonIjBSMxSQksWNL0PjEorEBrnOIJxxD7YuZV2+GocQco1uELlEQlxEyTjkcQqFJWF6JUUqFaMyp41eV084pWXVGZ7zw0Lo1ReIrxgE","title":"open-thoughts/AgentTrove · Datasets at Hugging Face","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/open-thoughts/AgentTrove"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — huge, but synthetic and single-turn-user.\n  - ","nativeMessageIdx":3},{"type":"text","text":"A small MCP trajectory benchmark with 3-5 turn conversations, including 11 multi-turn trajectories captured from real agent sessions","nativeMessageIdx":3,"citations":[{"type":"web_search_citation","cited_text":"✅ Multi-turn conversations — 3-5 turns per agent with escalating complexity · ✅ Diverse domains — 38 agents across 6 business verticals · ✅ Complete a...","encrypted_index":"EpEBCioIExgCIiRkNTg3NDcwNC1iMWQxLTQ3YmYtYTFhMC1jNWI5MDRkZjA0ZjgSDNxqMsZ6OoaCw3zeiRoM+pOi94pxSsDbWWQ9IjCAOKdZqeRt0tDEiUExuhgWXsnhYeUp2UykWKcCfDUosV35C+NEAkTX51/TeuDeEaoqFUUCTvN9XgIoH3STqr8gmi1bn/uKZBgE","title":"obaydata/mcp-agent-trajectory-benchmark · Datasets at Hugging Face","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/obaydata/mcp-agent-trajectory-benchmark"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — closest in shape to your harness, but tiny and business-vertical flavored.\n\nMy read: use WildVis to hand-pick 2-3 long WildChat sessions where a confused user is grinding on an unfamiliar problem, then hand-splice in plausible tool calls to fit your harness format. The human confusion is the hard part to fake; tool calls are the easy part.","nativeMessageIdx":3}],"stopReason":"end_turn","usage":{"inputTokens":6,"outputTokens":1246,"cacheHits":48094,"cacheMisses":17417}}}
